                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "34ecad94-9c20-39d6-bccb-a5b04acefe0c",
                        "entry_id": "a1ba5fc2-8d92-3f8e-883f-0e7858de0d48",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Buch"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "mittelbairisch"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e1c7c844-85fb-4f80-87cc-fed0c68aced8",
                                "sense_id": "34ecad94-9c20-39d6-bccb-a5b04acefe0c",
                                "text": "Wås liesdn då gråd fiar a Buach?",
                                "translation": "Welches Buch liest du gerade eben?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d49b586e-c2ee-43ea-815b-17ce67ddedae",
                                "sense_id": "34ecad94-9c20-39d6-bccb-a5b04acefe0c",
                                "text": "Schauts sagt da Franz, i hab dahoam / A Büachl, da stehts d'rin, / Daß's höchsti Zeit is, daß i nach / Amerika ziag hin!\n So, sagt da Landrichta, dös is / Wohl a verbot'ns Buach, / Glei sagst das, wia dös hoaßt, sunst kimm / I hin zu dir, und suach.\n Schau hätt's nöd denkt, daß unsa Franz / Gar is a Democrat, / Und daß er solche Sach'n treibt, / Verbot'ne Büacha hat."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c5a3377d-fdc6-43bb-a4d4-c0abb49c021b",
                                "sense_id": "34ecad94-9c20-39d6-bccb-a5b04acefe0c",
                                "text": "Bilder und Büacha hobn s' [= die oldn Griachn] gmocht, wia ma s' heunt noh gern onschaut, und Häuser und Templ hobn s' aufbaut, daß s nix zweits meh gibt."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "008b02d6-f077-4a72-a140-3b6c02db2b33",
                        "source_entry_id": "a1ba5fc2-8d92-3f8e-883f-0e7858de0d48",
                        "source_sense_id": "34ecad94-9c20-39d6-bccb-a5b04acefe0c",
                        "source_sense_description": "mittelbairisch: Buch",
                        "target_lang_word": "book",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "book",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "76694d0e-312c-3600-8d76-d7a313d6fe66",
                                        "entry_id": "4bf39dba-84cd-316f-82f2-027a5636f99c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A collection of sheets of paper bound together to hinge at one edge, containing printed or written material, pictures, etc."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fd4fdc03-ccb3-4e89-a3bf-b061ab2b30fd",
                                                "sense_id": "76694d0e-312c-3600-8d76-d7a313d6fe66",
                                                "text": "Knowing I lou'd my bookes, he furniſhd me / From mine owne Library, with volumes, that / I prize aboue my Dukedome."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "21531927-b416-452c-97d4-0f18f65da265",
                                                "sense_id": "76694d0e-312c-3600-8d76-d7a313d6fe66",
                                                "text": "I repeat: it suffices that a book be possible for it to exist. Only the impossible is excluded. For example: no book can be a ladder, although no doubt there are books which discuss and negate and demonstrate this possibility and others whose structure corresponds to that of a ladder."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a2f65d42-3b10-4faf-87e4-4da9aa63c1e4",
                                                "sense_id": "76694d0e-312c-3600-8d76-d7a313d6fe66",
                                                "text": "I can be anything.\nTake a look!\nIt's in a book:\nA reading rainbow."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ccac24f9-d159-4d4a-9c5b-d1805a329b2d",
                                                "sense_id": "76694d0e-312c-3600-8d76-d7a313d6fe66",
                                                "text": "Trefusis's quarters could be described in one word. Books. Books and books and books. And then, just when an observer might be lured into thinking that that must be it, more books... Trefusis himself was highly dismissive of them. ‘Waste of trees,’ he had once said. ‘Stupid, ugly, clumsy, heavy things. The sooner technology comes up with a reliable alternative the better... The world is so fond of saying that books should be “treated with respect”. But when are we told that words should be treated with respect?’"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9f093945-29c5-4d65-8b85-5fe01baff35a",
                                                "sense_id": "76694d0e-312c-3600-8d76-d7a313d6fe66",
                                                "text": "She opened the book to page 37 and began to read aloud."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eb0fc153-f559-4088-839d-e4ba6c736f76",
                                                "sense_id": "76694d0e-312c-3600-8d76-d7a313d6fe66",
                                                "text": "He was frustrated because he couldn't find anything about dinosaurs in the book."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a7d23ded-1953-3d2e-8a66-227e4d639996",
                                        "entry_id": "4bf39dba-84cd-316f-82f2-027a5636f99c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A long work fit for publication, typically prose, such as a novel or textbook, and typically published as such a bound collection of sheets, but now sometimes electronically as an e-book."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1e1c0a17-2bc0-4c35-8833-a237bf4af811",
                                                "sense_id": "a7d23ded-1953-3d2e-8a66-227e4d639996",
                                                "text": "I have three copies of his first book."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ef4a01b5-5dba-4718-bdca-f09379d530b8",
                                                "sense_id": "a7d23ded-1953-3d2e-8a66-227e4d639996",
                                                "text": "“I would never read a book,” he once told an interviewer. “I don’t want to say no book is ever worth reading, but I actually do believe something pretty close to that.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2bd1cc4a-7285-4482-854a-d299f7c9b13f",
                                                "sense_id": "a7d23ded-1953-3d2e-8a66-227e4d639996",
                                                "text": "They read some books\nSharing their moods\nThey know everything\nWhatever it can mean"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "97c7d092-0b34-3180-ac93-bd7e9ae2727a",
                                        "entry_id": "4bf39dba-84cd-316f-82f2-027a5636f99c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A major division of a long work."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4c381dc4-ab97-4a0d-834a-4ba6ef16e437",
                                                "sense_id": "97c7d092-0b34-3180-ac93-bd7e9ae2727a",
                                                "text": "Genesis is the first book of the Bible."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0256a856-b2d6-4527-9554-e1ed023ec5b6",
                                                "sense_id": "97c7d092-0b34-3180-ac93-bd7e9ae2727a",
                                                "text": "Many readers find the first book of A Tale of Two Cities to be confusing."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c5adac15-9900-395c-88d8-8fe32a9e80d0",
                                        "entry_id": "4bf39dba-84cd-316f-82f2-027a5636f99c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A record of betting (from the use of a notebook to record what each person has bet)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "453accfc-264b-4357-82da-00389027217c",
                                                "sense_id": "c5adac15-9900-395c-88d8-8fe32a9e80d0",
                                                "text": "I'm running a book on who is going to win the race."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f86d94ac-27e8-32c0-8596-826811d392df",
                                        "entry_id": "4bf39dba-84cd-316f-82f2-027a5636f99c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A bookmaker (a person who takes bets on sporting events and similar); bookie; turf accountant."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6ae728dd-ac6e-38df-aef0-398e76e50b1a",
                                        "entry_id": "4bf39dba-84cd-316f-82f2-027a5636f99c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A convenient collection, in a form resembling a book, of small paper items for individual use."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9ebc97c4-9bfc-400d-8cc3-1661b1db9aaa",
                                                "sense_id": "6ae728dd-ac6e-38df-aef0-398e76e50b1a",
                                                "text": "a book of stamps"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3fb6355f-baf1-47b1-9fa3-3206ca98d0f9",
                                                "sense_id": "6ae728dd-ac6e-38df-aef0-398e76e50b1a",
                                                "text": "a book of raffle tickets"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0dcc8681-3eb3-4f67-9b71-a37aae7745cf",
                                                "sense_id": "6ae728dd-ac6e-38df-aef0-398e76e50b1a",
                                                "text": "a book of matches (matchbook)"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "46572b5c-a64e-3b9b-979b-d4b5b41aeb08",
                                        "entry_id": "4bf39dba-84cd-316f-82f2-027a5636f99c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The script of a musical or opera."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6257f111-aa81-4600-8a05-82b253f5379d",
                                                "sense_id": "46572b5c-a64e-3b9b-979b-d4b5b41aeb08",
                                                "text": "The guild helps ensure that the ownership and control of the music, lyrics, and book of a show remain in the hands of its authors and composers—not the producers."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b884d532-c9d0-32d7-b7bc-418e3b3eb7f8",
                                        "entry_id": "4bf39dba-84cd-316f-82f2-027a5636f99c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Records of the accounts of a business."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "plural-normally"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "118a45dc-a027-3727-86b3-c985d4ee367f",
                                        "entry_id": "4bf39dba-84cd-316f-82f2-027a5636f99c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A book award, a recognition for receiving the highest grade in a class (traditionally an actual book, but recently more likely a letter or certificate acknowledging the achievement)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "colloquial"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
